==English==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|suppressus|lang=la}}, perfect passive participle of {{term|supprimō||press down or under|lang=la}}, from {{term|sub||under|lang=la}} + {{term|premō||press|lang=la}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/səˈpɹɛs/|lang=en}}
* {{audio|En-us-suppress.ogg|Audio (US)|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɛs|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|sup|press|lang=en}}

===Verb===
{{en-verb|suppresses|suppressing|suppressed}}

# to [[put an end to]], especially with force, to [[crush]], [[do away with]]; to [[prohibit]], [[subdue]]
#: ''Political dissent was brutally '''suppressed'''.
# to [[restrain]] or [[repress]] an [[expression]]
#: ''I struggled to '''suppress''' my smile.
# {{context|psychiatry|lang=en}} to [[exclude]] undesirable thoughts from one's mind
#: ''He unconsciously '''suppressed''' his memories of abuse.''
# to [[prevent]] publication
#: ''The government '''suppressed''' the findings of their research about the true state of the economy.''
# to stop a [[flow]] or [[stream]]
#: ''The rescue team managed to '''suppress''' the flow of oil by blasting the drilling hole.''
#: ''Hot blackcurrant juice mixed with honey may '''suppress''' cough.
# {{context|US|legal|lang=en}} to [[forbid]] the use of [[evidence]] at [[trial]] because it is [[improper]] or was improperly obtained
# {{context|electronics|lang=en}} to [[reduce]] unwanted frequencies in a signal
# {{context|obsolete|lang=en}} to [[hold]] in place, to keep [[low]]

====Related terms====
* [[suppression]]
* [[suppressor]]

